{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Why do you cry to Me.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the word אלי, 'to Me,' means — the matter does not depend on Me but on Israel. <b>Speak to the children of Israel</b> — that the sea is destined to split before them, and let them trust and immediately journey on." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the word אלי is like the word לי mentioned in the section of Terumah, as they expounded upon it in the Book of the Bahir (Exodus 25:2): ״ויקחו לי תרומה״ — ויקחו לי\"ו ד תרומה, and the word alludes that prayer and outcry are only to the specific Name; therefore He said, 'Speak to the children of Israel and let them journey' — from below upward, and then the sea would split; but supplication belongs to the attribute of judgment, and understand this. Now Moses did so: he informed Israel of this great sign, and they trusted in it and journeyed immediately. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said that the tribe of Judah sanctified the Name and entered the sea first, as it says in the Midrash (Psalms 114:2): ״בצאת ישראל ממצרים וגו׳, היתה יהודה לקדשו״ — Israel, his dominions — this teaches that the tribe of Judah sanctized the Holy One, blessed be He, first; and this is what is written (ibid.): ״הים ראה וינוס״ — the sea saw and fled. What did it see? Nahshon son of Amminadav, who leaped first into the sea; and the other tribes were contending with him, each wanting to enter first; and the tribe of Benjamin wanted to go down into the sea first, as it says (Psalms 68:28): ״שם בנימין צעיר רדם״ — do not read רודם but רד ים; and his brothers the children of Judah were pelting them with stones, as it says (ibid.): ״שרי יהודה רגמתם, שרי זבולון שרי נפתלי״ — that is, they were contending with the princes of Zebulun and with the princes of Naphtali. Now Judah prevailed over his brothers, for Nahshon leaped into the sea first; therefore, Israel, his dominions — the dominions of Judah. And they further said in the Midrash that for this reason the prince of the tribe of Judah was called נחשון, on account of his going down first into the נחשול (wave) of the sea."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:59.489615758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}